[{:seon.task/name "one-documented-config"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-21: \"the only things that should stay are documented config schemas that we are porting from seon if they are relevant. Is aero and our config system working?\" Found: aero 1.1.6 read only system.edn; seon.config held 16 config keys as literals each read from SEON_* at load; ~38 more System/getenv calls with inline defaults sat in 14 files (root store/backend/provider, agent trip/heap/key, sock buffer, LMDB map, web port and public dir, contract instrumentation, lib probe path, my.root and contract JOLT_PWD, ui UTC offset, check soak/swarm switches, e2e provider); reconcile and print held more config keys as literals; system.clj and web.clj baked the checkout path at compile time, so a worktree's binary reused next/'s path from the shared AOT cache. Done: resources/seon/config/default.edn (v1's shape: unit, provenance, bound beside every key), validated by :seon.config/config (resources/seon/schemas/seon.config*.edn, closed map; v1 keys ported where relevant) when seon.config loads at boot; #env only where a script sets one; #profile by SEON_PROFILE (:deepseek for the paid model); #seon/checkout derives checkout paths at load from SEON_CHECKOUT (bin/env exports it) or JOLT_PWD (jolt run); the only System/getenv calls in src are seon.config's checkout, profile and secret; root writes the config in force on main's root entity (seon.config/facts with root's boot fact; platform records, never merged); seon.config/from-db reads it on main or a branch; the dashboard shows it by the schema's declared render (seon.render.ui/config-panel). Classified with FENCES and the owner's ruling (2026-10-21: no clocks or timers decide anything, so no key in ms or s): the agent stop bound, the stall silence, the flush window and the model HTTP timeout are guards, not keys: named defs in their owners (seon.agent-proc/stop-bound-ms and stall-ms, seon.db/flush-ms, seon.model's :timeout-ms) left for seon.root/shutdown-and-death-are-dataflow, seon.fences/a-stall-is-past-the-requests-own-bound, seon.root/one-clock and seon.fences/a-transient-model-failure-parks; the checks that move the stall and the flush window pass them to root's start! as arguments (no SEON_STALL_MS/SEON_FLUSH_MS); SEON_FX_DIRECT (an off experiment), SWARM_DEBUG, SEON_STORE, SEON_BACKEND, SEON_SYSTEM, SEON_WEB_PUBLIC env overrides went (no user); soak's SOAK_* switches became mode arguments. Layers (owner: \"hand out different edn config files ... or do command line overrides\"): the shipped file, the checkout's own config/local.edn (gitignored; bin/ports writes its ports from ../worktree-ports, bin/worktree --remove frees the block), then --config FILE and --set :ns/key=edn from the command line (read from *command-line-args* while namespaces load; Jolt's jolt/argv binds it in built binaries), later winning key by key, validated once; seon.config/sources and the :seon.config/sources fact name each key's layer. No port is listened on unless the config says so (:seon.config.web/port and :seon.config.root/server-port ship 0). Octopus merges are off as decided (:seon.config.merge/max-running 1, written at boot: seon.fences/merge-trains-off-as-decided's fix)."
