 {:seon.task/name "config-tests-follow-the-shipped-thinking-default"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by session WPI (2026-10-21, `bin/test --reach` on main `663c5f5` plus the Jolt pin `be2495af`): main's `4e19e1f` ships `:seon.config.ai/thinking :disabled` in `resources/seon/config/default.edn`, but three tests still take it as set nowhere: `seon.config-test/a-key-the-config-lacks-is-refused-not-nil` and `seon.config-test/a-setting-set-nowhere-is-refused-not-nil` expect `(config/value :seon.config.ai/thinking)` refused (it now answers `:disabled`), and `seon.config-test/the-shipped-file-validates-under-every-profile` removes `:seon.config.ai/thinking` from the declared keys it expects the shipped file to set. Green at 20:03 in the shared results, red at 20:21. Correct: the two error tests use a key the shipped file really leaves unset, and the shipped-file test expects thinking set."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.config-test/a-key-the-config-lacks-is-refused-not-nil seon.config-test/a-setting-set-nowhere-is-refused-not-nil seon.config-test/the-shipped-file-validates-under-every-profile}}
 {:seon.task/name "schema-forms-baked-once"
  :seon.task/plan "Session DUP-HELPERS, audit row A8 (dead-code row 17). seon.config bakes resources/seon/schemas/seon.config*.edn at compile time (baked-schema-forms) and seon.contract bakes every resources/seon/schemas/*.edn again (schema-forms, baked-forms), so a binary carries the config forms twice and two readers of one directory can drift. seon.contract already requires seon.config: config bakes the whole directory once (schema-forms, every named form of the platform), its registry is built over it (a simple registry resolves only what :seon.config/config reaches), and seon.contract/forms is that map. seon.config owns schemas-dir; seon.source reads it there. Deletes about 12 lines."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.config-test/the-schema-forms-are-baked-once seon.config-test/the-shipped-file-validates-under-every-profile}}]
